        "title": "Docs: update free model picker defaults and catalog in READMEs",
        "summary": "The English and Chinese root READMEs refine the model picker table to specify which DeepSeek V4.1 row is the default for each access tier and plan state, replacing the generic 'the default' labels with tier-specific wording. The CLI release README is updated to match the current model catalog, removing retired and promotional models (GLM 5.3 Flash, MiMo v2.6 Flash Fast, Space Bunny Alpha, Gemini 4 Argon, GPT-6.1 Sol) and adding the current free experimental models (Beam 1.0, Nemotron 3.5 Lightning, Glyph Cluster). These documentation changes align the public references with the model picker state established by recent catalog updates, such as DeepSeek V4.1 Flash becoming the Freebuff default and fallback model.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "audience": "maintainers",
        "evidence": "In `README.md` and `README.zh-CN.md`, the model picker table rows for `DeepSeek V4.1 Flash`, `DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Slow`, and `DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Fast` are updated to clarify that `DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Fast` is the default at full access, `DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Slow` is the default at limited access without a plan, and `DeepSeek V4.1 Flash` is the default at limited access with a paid plan; in `freebuff/cli/release/README.md`, the full model list and FAQ are rewritten to remove retired models like `GLM 5.3 Flash`, `MiMo v2.6 Flash Fast`, `Space Bunny Alpha`, `Gemini 4 Argon`, and `GPT-6.1 Sol`, and to list the current catalog.",
        "userVisible": false,
